[38;5;231m⏺[39m Fixed.

  [1mRoot cause:[0m [38;5;153mgetDiscountRate[39m ([38;5;153msrc/pricing.js:15[39m) was a [3mpartial[0m lookup — [38;5;153mRATES[code][39m returns [38;5;153mundefined[39m for a code that
  isn't in the table. [38;5;153mfinalPrice[39m then computed [38;5;153mprice - price * undefined[39m, which is [38;5;153mNaN[39m, and [38;5;153mcheckout.js:11[39m rendered that
  NaN straight onto the receipt. The [38;5;153m__proto__: null[39m on [38;5;153mRATES[39m guarantees the miss is a clean [38;5;153mundefined[39m rather than an
  inherited [38;5;153mObject[39m member, so the miss always reaches the arithmetic.

  [1mFix:[0m one line at the origin — [38;5;153mRATES[code] ?? 0[39m, making the lookup total so an unknown code means "no discount." I did
  not patch [38;5;153mfinalPrice[39m or the receipt formatting; those were downstream symptoms, and guarding there would have left
  [38;5;153mgetDiscountRate[39m still handing [38;5;153mundefined[39m to any future caller.

  [1mVerified:[0m
  - Original repro now prints [38;5;153mTotal: $100.00[39m.
  - Known codes unchanged: [38;5;153mSAVE10[39m → 90, [38;5;153mSAVE20[39m → 80, [38;5;153mHALFOFF[39m → 50.
  - Edge cases covered: [38;5;153mundefined[39m code → 0, and [38;5;153m'toString'[39m → 0 (the null prototype prevents an inherited-member hit).
  - [38;5;153mnode src/index.js[39m still runs.

  The repo has no test framework or test directory, so I wrote the failing test as a scratch script at
  [38;5;153m/tmp/pricing-repro.js[39m rather than inventing a testing convention. It failed before the fix ([38;5;153mundefined !== 0[39m) and
  passes after. Say the word if you want it promoted into the repo as a real test file.

